From: knulli <knulli@knulli>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] compile the dmabuf path out when SDL has no wayland driver

SDL_SysWMinfo's union only carries its wayland member when SDL was built
with SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_WAYLAND, so DmabufOut::open() does not compile
against an SDL2 configured for fbdev or KMSDRM alone -- which is what the
mali handhelds (allwinner a133 and friends) ship.  Nothing is lost: no
window such an SDL creates could be a wl_surface, and display.cpp already
gates the whole scanline/dmabuf tier on the video driver being "wayland".

Signed-off-by: knulli <knulli@knulli>
---
diff --git a/src/frontend/sdl/display_wl.cpp b/src/frontend/sdl/display_wl.cpp
index 2ea5b99..1f7f20e 100644
--- a/src/frontend/sdl/display_wl.cpp
+++ b/src/frontend/sdl/display_wl.cpp
@@ -128,6 +128,14 @@ void DmabufOut::drop_buf(Buf& b) {
 }
 
 bool DmabufOut::open(SDL_Window* win, int w, int h, int output_index) {
+#ifndef SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_WAYLAND
+  // SDL was built without its wayland video driver -- an fbdev or a
+  // KMSDRM-only handheld build.  SDL_SysWMinfo then carries no wayland
+  // member at all, so the body below does not compile, and no window this
+  // SDL creates could ever be a wl_surface anyway.
+  (void)win; (void)w; (void)h; (void)output_index;
+  return false;
+#else
   if (!wldyn::load()) { std::fprintf(stderr, "dmabuf: no libwayland (%s)\n", wldyn::error()); return false; }
 
   SDL_SysWMinfo wm;
@@ -175,6 +183,7 @@ bool DmabufOut::open(SDL_Window* win, int w, int h, int output_index) {
     wl_region_destroy(r);
   }
   return true;
+#endif
 }
 
 void DmabufOut::close() {
